/**

@page documentation_tarch_visualisation_pyvista PyVista

PyVista can read many VTK files produced directly or indirectly from Peano
outputs. It is useful for scripted inspection, batch rendering, and lightweight
postprocessing workflows where opening a GUI is inconvenient.

*/

/**

@page documentation_tarch_visualisation_offline-conversion Offline conversion

Peano's native block output can be converted after a run into formats that are
easier to inspect with standard visualisation tools. This workflow is useful
when a simulation writes compact internal data first and a postprocessing stage
creates VTU/PVD or related files later.

*/

/**

@page documentation_tarch_visualisation_paraview ParaView

ParaView is the standard interactive tool for inspecting Peano and ExaHyPE
outputs. Open the generated `.pvd`, `.vtu`, `.xmf`, or converted output file
matching the solver's plotting configuration.

*/

/**

@page tarch_patch_file_format Patch file format

Peano's patch output represents Cartesian patches by their offset, size,
dimension, and associated cell or vertex data. Conversion tools can map this
patch-oriented data into common VTK formats for visualisation.

*/

/**

@page documentation_tarch_visualisation_probing-data Probing data

Point probes and history outputs are typically written as tabular data. They are
best inspected with plotting or data-analysis tools rather than volume
visualisation software.

*/
